.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH batten-board-check 1  batten 
.SH NAME
batten\-board\-check \- Refuse a board whose columns, graph or citations lie, and print the ready frontier
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbatten board check\fR [\fB\-\-issue\fR] [\fB\-\-cites\fR] [\fB\-\-refs\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Refuse a board whose columns, graph or citations lie, and print the ready frontier
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-issue\fR \fI<issue>\fR
Read this issue\*(Aqs payload from the capture store rather than stdin (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-cites\fR
Judge each payload\*(Aqs Ready\-block citations against the tree instead of the graph
.TP
\fB\-\-refs\fR
Judge the tree\*(Aqs clause citations against the payloads instead of the graph
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
